module System/Numerics

# ============================================================================
# The 128-bit fast phases of erf and erfc of B128, for the D128 transcendentals (D128Fast.rf). B128.erf and
# erfc themselves are Tessera's, through Ingrid.
# ============================================================================
# Three regions, each with a proven error bound carried in B128Fx:
# - |x| < 1/2: the Taylor series of erf in x^2, alternating but with every nested value positive.
# - 1/2 <= |x| < 10: the table value erfc(c) at the nearest c = i/32 corrected by the integral of
#   e^(-t^2) from c to x, a Taylor series of e^(-2ct - t^2) whose terms follow the recurrence of the
#   Gaussian (so no exp is needed), with erf = 1 - erfc.
# - 10 <= x < 106.5: the asymptotic series of e^(x^2) erfc(x) times e^(-x^2) from the CORE-MATH exp.
# Beyond those, erf is +-1 and erfc is 2 for x <= -10.

# For c = i/32 (i = 16 .. 320): the integral of e^(-2ct - t^2) over [0, h] is h S, S = sum_k b_k tau^k with
# tau = 32 h (|tau| <= 1/2) and b_k = (-1)^k H_k(c) / ((k + 1)! 32^k) (H_k the Hermite polynomials), in units of
# 2^-126, rounded to nearest from the exact rationals; each centre keeps the fewest terms whose rest is below
# half a unit. B128_ERFC_JOFF[i - 16] is where centre i starts (its terms run up to the next centre's start).
